    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d791">

                <pb facs="0751" n="635" xml:id="pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 894.001 M98/9.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 29, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You will make to the Government of Japan appropriate expressions of the sympathy
                    of the President, the Government and the people of the United States in the loss
                    by the Japanese Empire of a ruler whose reign has been so beneficent and
                    distinguished. This will be in addition to the messages which the President has
                    sent to the new Emperor and to the Empress Dowager, and my own cable to Viscount
                    Uchida.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
